--- Captured Modbus Robot Frame Analysis ---
  Line 1 (Ethernet II) -> Layer 2 (Data Link), PDU: Frame, 14B hdr + 4B FCS = 18B
  Line 2 (IPv4)        -> Layer 3 (Network),   PDU: Packet, 20B hdr, TTL 64 -> 61 => 3 routers crossed
  Line 3 (TCP)         -> Layer 4 (Transport), PDU: Segment, 20B hdr (Src 51522 -> Dst 502 Modbus)
  Line 4 (Data)        -> Layer 7 (App),       PDU: Data/Message, 12B payload
  Wire size (12B cmd)  : 70 bytes | Overhead = 58/70 = 82.86%
  Wire size (1400B cam): 1458 bytes | Overhead = 58/1458 = 3.98%
  Fault mapping        : (a) Wrong MAC -> L2 Data Link; (b) TTL=0 -> L3 Network; (c) Port closed -> L4 Transport

--- Alternative Concept: Raw Ethernet (EtherType 0x8892, no IP/TCP) ---
  Header bytes saved per command        : 40 bytes (20B IP + 20B TCP)
  Logical wire size                     : 70 B -> 30 B (padded to 64 B IEEE 802.3 min frame)
  Commands/sec freed (100 Mbps, 70B->64B): 16,741 cmd/s (or 238,095 cmd/s unpadded)
  Lost by dropping IP/TCP               : No L3 routing across subnets/plants, no congestion/flow control, no TCP ordering.
